         <title><![CDATA[GTA VI dubbed biggest game release of a generation, Toronto reacts]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/player/play/9.7427345?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/72c0c7c1-9818-48ea-8071-3c9dabb9b320,1794934672487/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C342%2C5542%2C3117%29%3B' alt='Streetcar passing and pedestrians on streets at a busy intersection with neon billboards advertising showing cartoon female and male characters and words that read: Grand Theft Auto.' width='620' height='349' title='The jumbo screens near Sankofa Square, in Toronto, display ads for Grand Theft Auto IV on Nov. 16, 2026. The latest instalment in the video game series launches worldwide on Nov. 19.'/><p>Over 17 million people have already pre-ordered GTA VI ahead of its release at midnight on Thursday. From billboards to lines outside storefronts, Toronto is clearly feeling the buzz. CBC's Nathan Abraha checks out why everyone is losing their minds over this release.</p>]]></description>
         <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:40:08 EST</pubDate>
